        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Checkmate',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Checkmate: Jordan/Palestine children's game. Crazy Eightsâ€“style; play by rank or suit. Aces force another player to give you a King. Red/black Jokers match any card of that colour. First out wins.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Jordan and Palestine. Children's game related to Crazy Eights: no wild suit card; Aces force another player to give the active player a King ('checkmate'). Red and black Jokers match any card of their colour.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '2, 3, or 4 players. Play anticlockwise. If dealer wins, deal passes right; otherwise same player deals again.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '52 cards plus 2 Jokers (one red, one black). 54 cards total.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "52-card pack + 2 Jokers; play area ('floor').",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '10 cards each, one at a time. Rest form face-down stock (fanned; any card may be drawn). Dealer leads first card to start play pile.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
